# Tables

Applies to `design/` mockups, `frontend/` production UI, and `backend/` list APIs.

## Pagination (required)

- Every data table / list view must paginate — do not render unbounded full-table rows
- Default page size: **10** (user-selectable **10 / 25 / 50 / 100**; persisted in design mockups via `sessionStorage` key `warehouse-design-page-size`)
- Controls: rows-per-page select + previous / next (icon) + showing range + page indicator; reset to page 1 when search, filters, or page size change
- Pager chrome uses i18n (th/en) — not hardcoded copy

**Design:** [`design/js/components/crud-list.js`](../../design/js/components/crud-list.js) — shared pager for module CRUD pages.

**Frontend:** paginate list/table components (e.g. server `page`/`limit` or client slice with the same UX).

**Backend:** list endpoints accept `page` + `limit` (or equivalent) and return total count for the pager.

## Default sort order

Apply **after** filters, **before** pagination.

| Table kind | Sort |
|------------|------|
| Self-FK **tree** (`tree_path` present — see design skill) | Group by `parent_id`; sort siblings `sort_order ASC → id ASC` **within each parent**; DFS pre-order (root `parent_id NULL` first). `tree_path` is for queries/indent only — not display order |
| Flat list with `sort_order` | `sort_order` ASC → `created_at` ASC |
| Neither | `created_at` ASC → `id` ASC (tiebreaker) |

- Geo `website_*` chain tables are flat lists (`sort_order` + `created_at`; typed parent FK, no `tree_path`)
- Optional custom `listCompare(a, b)` on a module config only for exceptional screens — avoid unless necessary

**Design:** sorting is centralized in `crud-list.js` (`sortRows`); remove per-page `.sort()` from `listRows` unless using `listCompare`.

**Backend:** tree list endpoints must return rows in the same hierarchical order (recursive CTE or app-level flatten per parent group). Do not rely on `ORDER BY tree_path` alone — sibling order follows `sort_order` under each `parent_id`, not lexicographic path labels.

## Drag-and-drop row reorder

Applies to **every list page / every table** in `design/`, `frontend/`, and reorder APIs in `backend/`.

- Enable drag-and-drop reorder **only** when the list’s base table has a `sort_order` column (flat list) or is a self-FK tree that uses `sort_order` for sibling order under each `parent_id`
- **No `sort_order` column:** no grip column, no drag-and-drop, do not write `sort_order` on reorder — use a normal table; default sort is `created_at → id` (see table above)
- **Design:** [`module-registry.js`](../../design/js/pages/module-registry.js) — set `sortable: true` only when `design/schema/<table>.sql` includes `sort_order`; otherwise `sortable: false` (example: `setting_vat`)
- **Frontend:** same rule when implementing list reorder UI
- **Backend:** no reorder endpoint that patches `sort_order` on tables that lack the column
- Column header sort (below) remains available on all data tables regardless of DnD

## Column header sort

Applies to `design/` mockups and `frontend/` production UI (when list tables ship).

- Every **data column** header is clickable and cycles **none → asc → desc → none** (third click clears)
- Default sort order (section above) applies only when **no** header sort is active
- **While a header sort is active, drag-and-drop reorder is disabled** — `sort_order` must only be rewritten from the default/`sort_order` view; keep the grip column visible but inert
- Not sortable: grip/drag column, actions column
- Reset to page 1 when sort changes (same as search/filter)
- Design: [`design/js/components/crud-list.js`](../../design/js/components/crud-list.js) — sort icons from Lucide (`arrow-up-down`, `arrow-up`, `arrow-down`)

## Column alignment

Applies to `design/` mockups and `frontend/` production UI (list/table cells and headers).

### Numeric (right)

- **When:** columns that display pure numeric values (counts, quantities, money, percentages).
- **Design:** `data-table__col-numeric` on `th`/`td` (use `.data-table td.data-table__col-numeric` in CSS so alignment beats default `.data-table td { text-align: left }`); sortable headers also use `data-table__sort-col` (sort button aligns end — see `style.css`).
- **Frontend:** `text-right` + `tabular-nums` on header and cells.

### Center

- **When:** status switches/badges, composite non-text cells (e.g. warehouse label + button), **actions** (icon buttons).
- **Design:** `data-table__col-center` on centered data/sort headers and cells (compound selectors on `th`/`td` in CSS); **actions** use `data-table__actions-col` (header), `td.data-table__actions-cell` (or module width class) + inner `div.data-table__actions` (inline-flex, `gap: 0.375rem`) — do not put `display: flex` on the `td` itself.
- **Frontend:** `text-center` / flex center; action row matches design gap.

- Apply the **same alignment class(es)** to the column header (`th`) and body cells (`td`); use a shared column config (e.g. `class` + optional `cellClass` for actions) so header and body do not drift.

### Exceptions

- Mixed number + unit text (e.g. packaging): center or left — not forced right.
- Dates/datetimes: [dates rule](dates.mdc) — not numeric alignment.
- Default text columns: left.
